{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405870-i-love-the-chapter-fictions-so-much-i-wish-exalted-had-a-whole-novel-line","id":1405870,"title":"I love the chapter fictions so much I wish Exalted had a whole novel line.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-01T20:00:42-07:00","id":1405870,"title":"I love the chapter fictions so much I wish Exalted had a whole novel line.","content":"Firstly, whoever got the idea to ditch those comics and use short stories needs a raise. Even when they weren't embarrassingly puerile, the comics were just too short to really leave an impact. The ones that <i>are</i> good could be turned into even better chapter fictions. I am not joking when I say I'm excited for the upcoming and planned splats partially just to read the fictions. Exalted: one of the few RPG's nearly as fun to read as it is to play.<br /> <br /> But yes, I'm getting to my point. I would absolutely read Exalted novels. I know a few exist, but like...there is SO MUCH good stuff in Exalted, stuff I'd never approach even in my own games because there's way too much in there. I'd love to read a good author just take their time and write a big ol' set of books. Especially for places like Autochthonia (I know it will be years before we even get an inkling of that place existing or not), where the world is so fundamentally strange and weird that two supplements (an Alchemicals splat and a supplement on the setting itself) are just not enough. There's a lot of stuff in CoCD: Autochthonia where it's like &quot;oh and this thing exists moving on&quot; and I'm just &quot;NO TELL ME MORE PLEASE THAT WAS REALLY COOL AND INTERESTING&quot;<br /> <br /> And, likes, yes, I know. RPG novels aren't generally that good (though someone must be buying all those Pathfinder books clogging up the RPG section of my local Barnes and Noble) and the point of an RPG is to <i>play</i> it, but Exalted feels different to me, man. It's one of the few RPG's that both tries to make a really-fleshed out world (I own the Pathfinder corebook and could not tell you a single place in its canon world or even what said world's damn name is! Meanwhile I could tell you about the Realm--the <i>Realm alone</i>--for like six hours) and is big/popular enough to get lots of detail and lore written for it. If anything, it's one of the few RPG's that <i>can</i> support an entire novel without having to make up tons of stuff to compensate. Entire SERIES could be written taking place in Prasad, or in Whitewall, or in Yu-Shan, you get my point.<br /> <br /> I guess we can use this thread to throw around recommendations of fantasy novels with the same feel as Exalted, lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T20:19:32-07:00","id":1405873,"title":"","content":"Are the actual novels out for general purchase yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T20:21:41-07:00","id":1405874,"title":"","content":"I, too, have an inordinate amount of love for Exalted's fiction.<br /> <br /> \u200bMight I recommend 1e's <i>Caste Book</i> and <i>Aspect Book</i> lines? They explore the perspectives of a number of Solars and Dragon-Blooded from their perspective as members of X Caste/Aspect, as well as how others see them, and their memories of years long past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T08:19:40-07:00","id":1405946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405870-i-love-the-chapter-fictions-so-much-i-wish-exalted-had-a-whole-novel-line?p=1405873#post1405873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the actual novels out for general purchase yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>A few. For instance, the novella I wrote, The Silence Of Our Ancestors. There\u2019s also False Images, and the novel I co-wrote, Circle of Protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T10:01:16-07:00","id":1405956,"title":"","content":"TheCountAlucard is dead on with the Caste and Aspect books. Very good stuff.<br /> <br /> Also novel-wise, in previous editions there was There's A Day as Dark as Night, (<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1356/A-Day-Dark-as-Night-Exalted-1\" target=\"_blank\">apparently free right now?!</a>), Relic of the Dawn, In Northern Twilight, etc.<br /> <br /> Edit: I found them with this search on drivethru: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?keywords=exalted+novel&amp;x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=&amp;artist=&amp;pfrom=&amp;pto=\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....t=&amp;pfrom=&amp;pto=</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T11:00:42-07:00","id":1405966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405870-i-love-the-chapter-fictions-so-much-i-wish-exalted-had-a-whole-novel-line?p=1405946#post1405946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A few. For instance, the novella I wrote, The Silence Of Our Ancestors. There\u2019s also False Images, and the novel I co-wrote, Circle of Protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm definitely gonna recommend Circle of Protection. It's the only one of those I've gotten around to reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T11:10:29-07:00","id":1405970,"title":"","content":"Oh, I should have mentioned, I've read The Silence Of Our Ancestors, and greatly enjoyed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T15:10:02-07:00","id":1406006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405870-i-love-the-chapter-fictions-so-much-i-wish-exalted-had-a-whole-novel-line?p=1405966#post1405966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm definitely gonna recommend Circle of Protection. It's the only one of those I've gotten around to reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad! It's got more of a YA feel than my solo novella (which is more high-fantasy), so I think they can both serve as introductions to Creation for different types of readers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405870-i-love-the-chapter-fictions-so-much-i-wish-exalted-had-a-whole-novel-line?p=1405970#post1405970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I should have mentioned, I've read The Silence Of Our Ancestors, and greatly enjoyed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm pretty proud of it, and I think the novella-length helps keep the story tightly-focused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T11:33:57-07:00","id":1406474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405870-i-love-the-chapter-fictions-so-much-i-wish-exalted-had-a-whole-novel-line?p=1405946#post1405946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A few. For instance, the novella I wrote, The Silence Of Our Ancestors. There\u2019s also False Images, and the novel I co-wrote, Circle of Protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey so I bought CoP a few days ago and finally decided to read it last night before bed. I planned on reading like 20 pages or so...and stayed up till 3AM reading like half of it. I absolutely <i>adore</i> the novel!<br /> <br /> Firstly, Palym is an <i>adorable</i> bean and she is just so much fun to read. But secondly, I love the perspective it gives on Exaltation and especially Sids. Fandom discussions on them tend to focus on the Sids who are already familiar with their job and the stuff they do like &quot;omg a sid just punched my Solar and then avoidance kata'd away&quot; or Sids who are doing like fifteen different hilariously byzantine schemes and somehow have enough time for paperwork. But for me, one of my favorite parts of Exalted is newbie Exalts having no idea what to do with their power, and seeing Palym be this adorable dork who has no earth clue what the HECK she's doing is just really fun.<br /> <br /> The only flaw I have with this novel now is that it will eventually end. I hope you have a chance to write more Exalted stuff in the future!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T10:20:48-07:00","id":1406645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405870-i-love-the-chapter-fictions-so-much-i-wish-exalted-had-a-whole-novel-line?p=1406474#post1406474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only flaw I have with this novel now is that it will eventually end. I hope you have a chance to write more Exalted stuff in the future!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I appreciate that. Matt Forbeck gets the lion's share of the credit for the story and characters--CoP is a direct followup from his short story in the Ex3 fiction anthology. I helped give it that extra <i>Exalted </i>flair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}